  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">1. The Core Physics: Why Electricity Delivers 3x More Miles Per Dollar</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    To understand why EV charging is significantly cheaper than petrol refueling, one must look at thermodynamic conversion efficiency. An internal combustion engine is primarily a furnace that generates waste heat: only <strong>20% to 30%</strong> of the chemical energy contained in every liter of gasoline is converted into forward momentum at the wheels. The remaining 70% to 80% is lost through cooling systems, friction, and exhaust tailpipes.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    By contrast, modern electric motors in vehicles like the Tesla Model 3 or BYD Atto 3 convert <strong>88% to 94%</strong> of stored electrical energy directly into kinetic motion. Furthermore, regenerative braking recaptures up to 70% of vehicle momentum during deceleration, returning kilowatt-hours back into the battery instead of destroying brake pads.
  </p>

